WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.666
Hi! In a vocabulary cloze, a short passage has several blanks, and you choose the best word for each one. Today let's learn how to do it quickly and accurately.

2
00:00:12.816 --> 00:00:17.634
Step one: read the whole passage first, so you know what it's about.

3
00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:25.290
___ one: there was ___ rain. In English we say heavy rain, not strong rain, so the answer is A.

4
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:32.562
___ two: ___ our homework. We do homework, and the past tense is did. The answer is B.

5
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:37.794
___ three: we do the dishes, so the answer is B.

6
00:00:37.944 --> 00:00:45.690
Many blanks test collocations: words that usually go together in English. For example, make a decision.

7
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.170
Also make a mistake, and do the dishes.

8
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.938
Make a wish, do your best, and keep a secret.

9
00:00:53.088 --> 00:01:00.978
Make friends, do exercise, catch a cold. The more you read, the more familiar these become.

10
00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:07.866
When choosing, always look at the words just before and after the blank. They often decide the answer.

11
00:01:08.016 --> 00:01:14.202
The answer must make sense and also be grammatically correct, for example in tense and number.

12
00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:20.178
When you've finished, read the whole passage again to check that it flows.

13
00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:23.802
Watch out! Pay notice is wrong!

14
00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:29.610
Notice and attention have similar meanings, but English only says pay attention.

15
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:36.426
So when you choose, check not only the meaning but whether it goes with the words around it.

16
00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:46.290
Your turn! Please ___ a photo of us. Make, take or do? Pause and think.

17
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:53.490
The answer is take. Take a photo is a collocation. Did you get it right?

18
00:01:53.640 --> 00:02:03.570
Another one! I ___ a mistake in my spelling. Did, made or took? Pause and think.

19
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:09.450
The answer is made: make a mistake. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:19.914
Here's another! We were late because of the ___ traffic. Heavy, big or many? Pause and think.

21
00:02:20.064 --> 00:02:28.074
The answer is heavy. Heavy traffic means there are lots of cars on the road. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:38.778
One more! She always ___ her best in every test. Makes, does or takes? Pause and think.

23
00:02:38.928 --> 00:02:46.626
The answer is does. We say do your best, and with she we use does. Did you get it right?

24
00:02:46.776 --> 00:02:58.146
Remember: read the passage first, then look at the words around each blank. Choose the word that makes sense, is grammatical and collocates naturally. Then read it all again.

25
00:02:58.296 --> 00:03:03.114
Keep a little notebook of the collocations you learn!

